<section class="formula">
    <h2>The Mathematics of Aspect Ratio Calculation</h2>
    <p>An aspect ratio represents the proportional relationship between a rectangle width and height. It is expressed as <code>W : H</code>.</p>
    <p>To reduce any pixel resolution to its simplest whole-number ratio, divide both the width and height by their <strong>Greatest Common Divisor (GCD)</strong>:</p>
    <p><code>Ratio Width = Width / GCD(Width, Height)</code><br><code>Ratio Height = Height / GCD(Width, Height)</code></p>
    <p>To calculate a missing dimension while preserving the aspect ratio:</p>
    <p><code>New Height (H2) = New Width (W2) × (Original Height / Original Width)</code><br><code>New Width (W2) = New Height (H2) × (Original Width / Original Height)</code></p>
</section>

