<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What is an aspect ratio?</h3>
    <p>An aspect ratio is the proportional relationship between the width and height of an image, video frame, or display screen. It describes the shape of the rectangle rather than its physical size or pixel count.</p>

    <h3>What aspect ratio is 1920 x 1080?</h3>
    <p>1920 x 1080 pixels is a 16:9 aspect ratio. Dividing both 1920 and 1080 by their greatest common divisor (120) yields 16 and 9.</p>

    <h3>What is the difference between resolution and aspect ratio?</h3>
    <p>Resolution specifies the total number of pixels along the width and height (e.g., 3840x2160 pixels). Aspect ratio specifies the proportion between width and height (e.g., 16:9). Different resolutions like 1280x720, 1920x1080, and 3840x2160 all share the exact same 16:9 aspect ratio.</p>

    <h3>Which aspect ratio should I use for social media video?</h3>
    <p>For horizontal YouTube videos and desktop browsing, use 16:9 (1920x1080). For mobile vertical video platforms like TikTok, YouTube Shorts, and Instagram Reels, use 9:16 (1080x1920).</p>
